   "native_text": "Every evening, Elias climbed the spiral stairs to light the lamp. The sea was his only companion now. One grey dawn, a bottle rolled onto the rocks, sealed with crimson wax. Inside, a child's handwriting: *\"To the man in the tower\u2014are you real? Draw a star if you are.\"* Elias smiled for the first time in months. He painted a huge white star on the lighthouse wall. Weeks later, another bottle arrived: *\"I saw it! My name is Lily.\"* So began their correspondence\u2014messages tossed into the tide, two lonely souls finding each other across the water.<\uff5cend\u2581of\u2581sentence\uff5c>",
